+/* ---- body_sph (0x3271a8): the rain's drops on the body parts (task #165, rain_study.md section 8) ----
+   Per part the act (0x3275b8-0x327858) copies the part's n vertices to the scratchpad at 0x70000300 and its normals to 0x70002180 (16
+   bytes each, the game's qword copy behind S_w00a_P33bd38), copies the part's matrix to 0x1b99f0 (P125a78), turns the normals in place
+   with VU0 (P125f78), then from the first vertex on dots each turned normal with the rain direction at sp (P165de0, VU0), keeps the dot
+   in the normal's w and, for a dot above 0.7, places a drop: the vertex through the matrix (P125f18, VU0) into the drop buffer at r16,
+   three draws of the stage seed add (u - 1) x 80 to its x, y and z, and its packet entry (r18 + 6) gets 24; at 16 drops the loop stops,
+   and the slots left get 0 at +6.  nat_bs_part does one part natively: the VU0 operations are the translation's in the same order (on
+   the PSP the same VFPU instructions, on x86 the VFPU's rounding through vu_rnmul / vu_rnadd), the draws and float operations the same,
+   and it leaves the registers, the VU0 registers, memory and the virtual time at 0x327858 as the translation does.  It takes the
+   translation (returns 0) when an access is not plain RAM, a range it writes meets one it reads, the count is outside 1..488, a VU0 result
+   is a NaN or infinity (the translation's fallback then gives the VU0 model's value), or a poll in the part would reach k_poll_at.  Only
+   with g_opt2's OPT2_NBS (16384, this tree's runtime/host_time.h). */
